What is Perfluoroelastomer (FFKM)?
Perfluoroelastomer (FFKM) is a class of fluorinated synthetic rubbers characterized by a fully fluorinated polymer backbone that delivers unparalleled resistance to heat, chemicals, and radiation. Unlike conventional elastomers, FFKM does not degrade in the presence of strong acids, bases, solvents, or plasma environments, making it the material of choice for sealing components that operate in extreme process conditions. Typical product forms include O Rings, gaskets, V Rings, and custom molded seals that are used across a broad spectrum of high value industries.
